# Top-level runtime dependencies of the worker image. Edit this file, never requirements.txt.
#
# requirements.txt is the lock the Dockerfile installs: every package, transitive ones included,
# pinned to one version with its sha256 hashes (pip --require-hashes). The same source tree
# therefore always installs the same packages, whenever and wherever the image is rebuilt.
# After editing this file, regenerate the lock (tests/test_ci_pipeline.py fails if they disagree):
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --python-version 3.12 --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 --generate-hashes -o requirements.txt
